{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And Moses went out and spoke, etc.</b> He put the matters to the people first, and afterward gathered the elders — which is not what we find in the order of HaShem's words to him, where He put the gathering of the elders first and afterward ״וְאֶל הָעָם תֹּאמַר״ (Numbers 11:18). This is because [Moses] reasoned in his own mind that the supersonic will was to put his address to Israel first, for had his intention been to put the gathering first, he would not have been commanded [to deliver] the message to the people; rather, this very thing tells us that he would put the address to the people first and afterward gather the elders to the Tent and do everything stated in the matter." "<b>And the reason</b> that HaShem put the matter of the gathering first is that in this there would be a response to Moses' words, when he said ״לֹא אוּכַל לְבַדִּי לָשֵׂאת אֶת כָּל הָעָם״; therefore He prefaced by answering him regarding his words first, and afterward commanded him to speak to the children of Israel. And HaShem knew that Moses was wise enough to know what needed to come first — as indeed he acted with understanding." "It is further possible to say that the statement <b>and he spoke to the people the words of HaShem</b> refers only to the matter of gathering the elders, and he planned that once he finished what HaShem commanded regarding the gathering of the elders he would go out to speak to the people a second message — ״וְאֶל הָעָם תֹּאמַר״. And this is also implied by the words of Midrash Tanchuma."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:49.565139164Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}